{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line","id":1506777,"title":"If OPP couldn't make new CofD content, should they make a new Urban Fantasy line?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-28T12:28:46-07:00","id":1506777,"title":"If OPP couldn't make new CofD content, should they make a new Urban Fantasy line?","content":"If OPP were not greenlit by WW/Paradox to make any more CofD content would you support a new Urban Fantasy line? What changes would you hope to see?<br /> <br /> My Mechanical requests:<ul><li>Replace Extended Actions with a simpler system that takes less time.</li> <li>Improve on Social Maneuvering so that it works with the Skill's system better.</li> <li>Improve the Investigation system so that it works with the Skill's system better.</li> <li>Include Touchstones to all Splats.</li> <li>Codify Horror rules across all Antagonists types with Templates that differentiate how each Antagonist behaves from one another. (Like how Stix have Shadow Form, Pandorans can go Dormant, Cryptids have Aether sense, etc...)</li> </ul>My gameline requests:<ul><li>Codify faction and sub-type rules. Especially Geist/Sin-Eater whose Factions aren't factions, but Krewe types which makes them feel like they are missing faction depth.</li> <li>Give Demons a culture that allows them to interact with one another outside of Agencies.</li> <li>Rework Beasts to be more about supplementing their urges to do harm into positive change; if we are sticking with &quot;Lessons&quot; there needs to be a society that enforces these ideals. Can't just have a line that states Beasts frown upon killing prey, but then have a line that says leaving dead prey in public spaces is seen as good because it &quot;sends a message&quot;.</li> <li>Codify the Cosmology in a way that allows each Splat to be separate from one another if they so choose.</li> <li>Codify what Dreams, the Astral, the Primordial Dream, and Bastions are. So far it seems like synonyms for one another without a rhyme or reason.</li> <li>Give Vampires enough starting Disciplines to match other Splats that start with around 4-6 dots worth of Abilities.</li> <li>Allow for the origins of Splats to be obfuscated from them in lore and hearsay.</li> <li>Clarify the mechanics of Mages in a way that is less up to interpretation than MtAw currently is. Its tough to run a game when a system is so free form that a basic rules call like when to call for Acts of Hubris or Paradox changes with whoever is Storytelling the game at the time.</li> </ul>I probably have more, but I think this is a good place to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T14:39:40-07:00","id":1506790,"title":"","content":"I mean, they kinda already have via Scion 2e. Trinity 2e isn't hard to give a more urban fantasy edge instead of a speculative fiction edge if you want to do so.<br /> <br /> Given Trinity 2e a supplement along the lines of JL: Dark or the Midnight Suns (which mixes the default superhero settings of DC and Marvel with more fantasy aspects) so it's not overtly competing with CofD or WoD, and I think a lot of people would be happy as it wouldn't be hard to use that to replicated WoD or CofD with those tools.<br /> <br /> A lot of what you're asking for it too tied to the CofD for Onyx Path to actually do if they started their own UF game and would jeopardize their relationship with Paradox regarding any future WoD and Exalted books they get to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T16:21:03-07:00","id":1506800,"title":"","content":"So, are you suggesting a new [insert descriptor here] of Darkness, with revamped set of Gamelines? I can\u2019t imagine that any of the more niche games would make the jump. Mage, Werewolf, and Vampire would definitely make it, and I can\u2019t imagine Changeling wouldn\u2019t get a very similar successor, given how much everyone seems to love it. But everything else? Well, look at the differences between World and Chronicles. Quite the gap, even if the gamelines bear a similar sounding name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T18:56:31-07:00","id":1506813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line#post1506777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Mechanical requests:</div> </div> </div> </div>I note with some trepidation how quickly this moved from &quot;things we'd like to see&quot; to &quot;things I am asking for.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Replace Extended Actions with a simpler system that takes less time. </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what this is supposed to mean. The Extended Action rules are currently &quot;accumulate this many successes in this many rolls, failing a roll means you need to take a negative Condition to continue, succeeding exceptionally lets you make greater progress or otherwise improve the final result.&quot; It's specifically there for long-term projects that you can put down and pick up later or for time-sensitive activities for which how much time the process takes matters. The latest presentation of the Extended Action rules fits on a single page with space to spare.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Improve on Social Maneuvering so that it works with the Skill's system better.<br /> Improve the Investigation system so that it works with the Skill's system better. </div> </div> </div>I do not understand what these are supposed to mean. Skills are a source of dice and used in both of these systems already.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Include Touchstones to all Splats. </div> </div> </div>The splats that do not have Touchstones are either plain vanilla mortals or operating in a framework where &quot;you have a strong connection to another character&quot; is redundant with something they already have a subsystem for, or else they're Prometheans who don't get guaranteed abiding mortal connections as a splat-level assumption because of what that game is about.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Codify faction and sub-type rules. Especially Geist/Sin-Eater whose Factions aren't factions, but Krewe types which makes them feel like they are missing faction depth. </div> </div> </div>Because they are. Because Sin-Eater factions aren't a thing. The splat has had an unmetered global presence for barely more than a hundred years, it's not going to have anything with the institutional weight of the Diamond or the Invictus.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Give Demons a culture that allows them to interact with one another outside of Agencies. </div> </div> </div>They have that. That's what the Agendas and Tempter associations are about. Lots of demons <i>don't trust Agencies</i> because organized gatherings feel like tempting fate, but the Unchained are generally willing to extend enough trust to interact with other demons on at least a passing basis.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Codify the Cosmology in a way that allows each Splat to be separate from one another if they so choose. </div> </div> </div>I do not understand what this is supposed to mean. The setting as-presented quietly operates under the assumption that any given chunk of the supernatural is not ubiquitous enough for it to have to be sharing territory with any given other chunk of the supernatural, hence why most of the books that aren't multi-splat focused make little to no reference to other monsters in their sample city sections unless it's a story hook.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Codify what Dreams, the Astral, the Primordial Dream, and Bastions are. So far it seems like synonyms for one another without a rhyme or reason. </div> </div> </div>I do not think you have read any of the books these terms come from, because these terms are codified. Dreams are dreams. The Astral is the inside of the soul, which dreams touch the shallows of. The Primordial Dream is the part of the Astral between the soul of humanity as a collective and the soul of the rest of the world; the Horrors of Beasts dwell there. Bastions are the physical structures through which dreams can be accessed, which bleed some of their contents into their surroundings along the Dreaming Roads, which are hidden within the Hedge.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Give Vampires enough starting Disciplines to match other Splats that start with around 4-6 dots worth of Abilities. </div> </div> </div>Disciplines are built as scaled ladders of monstrosity whose starting powers were explicitly designed to be The Main Thing The Power Does, and they're selectable kit for a splat who can universally make people addicted to them, boost their Physical dicepools, and shrug off being shot multiple times/instantly heal damage it takes multiple days for mortals to heal. Even the Disciplines that aren't clan-specific include free kit like always-on stat boost, psychic invisibility, or making animals do stuff for you.<br /> <br /> Mages get six dots of Arcana because the first dot of any given Arcanum is very limited in what they can do, the second dot seldom adds much more, and their base spellcasting pool is built solely from Gnosis + Arcanum with very limited space for Yantras at low Gnosis. Specializing in an Arcanum to start at three dots means you have relatively little you can do with one of your other two, and spreading yourself thin to start with dots in five Arcana means you have one Mage Armor and a bunch of Compelling effects to complement your suite of investigatory spells.<br /> <br /> Demons likewise start with four Embeds because Embeds are very limited tricks that only scale in the sense that they serve as prerequisite for Exploits, which demons get as starting kit only by trading starting Embeds and semantically linking them to Embeds they know; all their obvious tricks burn Aether, risk Willpower, or shred Cover, and their subtle tricks are mostly there to help them move among mortals more easily<br /> <br /> Changelings start with four Common Contracts and two Royal Contracts because Contracts also don't scale more than the moderate/major power dichotomy (besides Goblin Contracts being more specific) and are operating under the same &quot;this is one trick&quot; model that Embeds and Exploits use; also literally none of them are unconditionally free to use and running out of Glamour makes them start to starve.<br /> <br /> Mummies start with four Affinities for the same &quot;this is a basic trick&quot; reason and have their Utterances constrained by their Sekhem and the cost in Pillars, but also their default assumptions of play are that they're the core of a cult serving a punishing demon-god that will pull the plug on their Sekhem if they start getting ideas above their station; their template combining undead resilience with supercharged regeneration along with a cult to help them and a tomb to be secure in, plus the fact that they need a specific Affinity to not risk wigging non-cultists out, exists completely divorced from their selection of starting powers.<br /> <br /> Prometheans get two powers with four effects each that cost three Pyros to fully use, and they <i>lose</i> those powers when they change focus unless they spend their primary Main Goal currency to keep them. The only way they get more is by completing story beats in the same supercategory of archetypal roles.<br /> <br /> Werewolves start with three Gift Facets and enough dots in Rites to learn the rite they need to keep their Harmony in check long-term, and being part of a pack is the main safety net to justify spending those dots on something else.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters start with three dots of Haunts, some Ceremonies that let them do their job and induct krewe members, and some other Ceremonies that they have to expand their krewe to unlock.<br /> <br /> Hunters start with some Tactics their cell is especially good at, plus two dots in Endowments or two unscaled Endowments, if they're playing characters with access to Endowments; they don't even get the extra starting Merit dots supernatural characters get.<br /> <br /> The Deviant template is literally just their Variations and the ways their powers fuck them up.<br /> <br /> A case could be made for putting some space into the Vampire template for starting with a Devotion or two, but Requiem is one of the gamelines where the PCs aren't assumed to be pooling resources on a shared project or serving otherworldly masters or pursuing occult knowledge \u2014 the core vampiric drive is survival as a human-shaped predator-parasite, and Disciplines are very good at that as-is.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Allow for the origins of Splats to be obfuscated from them in lore and hearsay. </div> </div> </div>This is already the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-28-2023, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T19:50:04-07:00","id":1506816,"title":"","content":"The opening post managed to jump right past it's actual premise and into &quot;What should a Chronicles 3rd Edition do?&quot; so hard, I feel like I need to offer a reorientation, so to that end, I think some questions that need to be answered for this are as follows:<br /> <br /> 1) Does the market at the time seem like it has the space for a new broad-scale urban fantasy/horror with monsters as the protagonist RPG to really flourish, or is now a bad time to introduce such?<br /> <br /> 1.5) Is the market hungry for an RPG that is Urban Horror first, Urban Fantasy second, or do they want that order of operations flipped, or the setting to hew strongly in one direction or the other?<br /> <br /> 2) Is there still an active interest in a shared RPG universe of strongly thematic gamelines that nevertheless share the same root systems and setting to allow for an &quot;Avengers&quot;* style crossover appeal, or is the market more interest in more hyper specific gamelines or settings that treat it all as soup? Is the World and Chronicles model too intensive of a model to follow in today's common buying practices, or do we think audiences are still receptive to that sort of investment?<br /> <br /> 3) What do we think the form is for this hypothetical urban fantasy/horror RPG that is discernably distinct from both World and Chronicles to warrant it's creation? What are it's overarching ideas and themes that inform different interpretations that aren't just repetitions of the prior two?<br /> <br /> 4) In terms of it's base system (and <i>just</i> it's base system, the basics of result determination), what are some assumptions that could be challenged or otherwise be chopped out or instituted that could arguably better facilitate the urban horror RPG as we understand it now versus both in 2013 and 2004? Are those concepts still versatile enough to work with mutliple distinct gamelines in a shared RPG universe?<br /> <br /> 5) How married to the particular expressions of each gameline should this thing be? Should there be a vampire, werewolf, wizard, fairy, ghost, hunter, mummy, and demon game, or should that format be re-examined and reconsidered?<br /> <br /> Because if we want to explore the question of if Onyx Path should do it's own version of these things, I think we need to get down to the bones of the question, rather than play around in the craft and structure level where, if direction were to be spun from, would only yield pale imitations.<br /> <br /> *Yeah, okay, fine, Monster Mashups have been done before the MCU Avengers took four genre strong movies and threw them in a blender, but more people are aware of that, so it's an easier comparison.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-28-2023, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T04:00:56-07:00","id":1506837,"title":"","content":"I would say no. I love Forsaken. And Deviant. But I'm not a fan of Vampire, and if they ended up having werewolves get a Vampire feel or even the same author I would be out of luck. And it's not like they would be able to port Forsaken over as is anyways, or that Deviant would be redone anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T13:37:09-07:00","id":1506869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather see second edition, which has very few books as it is relative to specific game lines more love. Rather than have to buy into an entire new system.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that Paradox just isn't approving books, so the question is more &quot;WOuld OPP be well advised to make their own, or is this entire concept not worth chasing anymore?&quot; CofD 2E is increasingly proving to be unlikely to move beyond it's last obligations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T19:08:17-07:00","id":1506906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1506869#post1506869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that Paradox just isn't approving books, so the question is more &quot;WOuld OPP be well advised to make their own</div> </div> </div> </div>uh. minor clarification question, do you mean their own setting, or books for second edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T19:45:25-07:00","id":1506915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1506906#post1506906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">uh. minor clarification question, do you mean their own setting, or books for second edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>New CofD books would require Paradox's approval, ergo this this thread can only be about their own Urban Fantasy setting. Which as Heavy conveniently stated in the first reply, does already exist in the form of Scion. Some of us even write for it. <br /> <br /> Also, what HA said about concepts being tied to CofD is really worth remembering. I want to make my own game/setting that I own at some point and while I love CofD and it will surely be in the DNA of what inspires me, it will end up being a very, very different game with different concepts. OPP especially could not just file the serial numbers off. And sincerely doubt anyone would want to make that game either, they'd want to make their own things instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T22:03:53-07:00","id":1506927,"title":"","content":"I would be very curious to find out exactly how close Paradox would let Onyx Path get to CofD 3e with the serial numbers filed off if Paradox isn't going to actually continue the CofD game line themselves. In my mind, it would actually be in Paradox's best interests to work with Onyx Path because there's an existing relationship to leverage. If some indie developer decides to make CofD with the serial numbers filed off because there's a market for it and the IP owners aren't catering to it... they could probably do all sorts of things Paradox would rather them not because RPGs are just too overlapping as products to fight too hard over infringement.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of talent out there that wants to work on CofD, and plenty of customers by indie RPG standards that clearly want it. At some point someone is going to make a RPG that draws CofD folks in if Paradox doesn't open up the spigot on their terms; even if that just means letting Onyx Path do something close-ish to it instead of letting them make books for it again.<br /> <br /> But then again, I continue to be baffled by Paradox's stance on the CofD. Even if they want to kill it to avoid competition for WoD5 (which it questionable since they can't stop other people from making urban fantasy play as the monsters RPGs), ripping off the band-aid and just telling us they're keeping ownership to use CofD for spare parts for WoD5 games lets us all move on instead of waiting with growing resentment as they leave things in limbo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 03-30-2023, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T15:45:47-07:00","id":1506995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1506915#post1506915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> New CofD books would require Paradox's approval, ergo this this thread can only be about their own Urban Fantasy setting. Which as Heavy conveniently stated in the first reply, does already exist in the form of Scion. Some of us even write for it.<br /> <br /> Also, what HA said about concepts being tied to CofD is really worth remembering. I want to make my own game/setting that I own at some point and while I love CofD and it will surely be in the DNA of what inspires me, it will end up being a very, very different game with different concepts. OPP especially could not just file the serial numbers off. And sincerely doubt anyone would want to make that game either, they'd want to make their own things instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I generally agree with Arms on the whole, I have to raise a sticking point that kind of hits on why some of the questions I suggested are the way they are-<br /> <br /> Scion is an urban mythic fantasy game, and Trinity is soft sci-fi with a modern superhero setting, among others. THese things can do urban horror, but it's not their center, and in this way, arguably neither are fulfilling the original ask, which is a Chronicles(/World)-like urban horror RPG of OPP's own.<br /> <br /> ....but then again, the original poster didn't frame Chronicles as urban horror either, or any kind of horror even. And I think that touches on a broader perspective that begs a question, because a <i>lot </i>of people have said they run Chronicles as an urban fantasy game, and not as a horror game-and a lot of people run into operational problems with Chronicles as a game <i>because</i> they're not running it with an understanding of it <i>as</i> horror.<br /> <br /> A minor example that is basically the issue in a nutshell is the complaint that you can't play Harry Dresden in Mage: the Awakening. It comes up a fair amount, and the take always misses that it's actually super easy to do that-most of Dresden's allies are supernatural entities of various scale who operate in similar fashion to the way things work in Awakening, most of his clients aren't on the scene for his work, and the closest exception to all of that is Murphy-who's not impossible, but whose concept is basically going to have their arc in the books done at a speed run. But, and this is the important part, it's easy to accept the small scale adjustments to the Dresden Files if you understand the work as leaning the entire series towards a horror interpretation. If you're just playing Mage as a flat way to get your fix of Dresden FIles style storytelling, then yeah, it's unsatisfying that your Murphy-alikes reach where she's at in Battle Ground in half the time, and it feels like you can't explore that sort of relationship (and I mean that beyond the burgeoning romance and more in the way that the supernatural and the human can interact).<br /> <br /> Stuff like that comes up all over the place-&quot;How do I play a good vampire?&quot;&quot;Does my Durance have to be absuive?&quot;&quot;What if I want Primordial Heroes to be motivated by goodness?&quot;, so on and so forth. A lot of people play Chronicles expecting it to be, at the risk of being really reductive, Dresden Files but Not Directly, and then run into problems and even get upset when it doesn't do that. Ordering a coffee and being upset it's not hot chocolate.<br /> <br /> So, if we're going to ask &quot;Should Onyx Path do it's own version of Chronicles?&quot;, I think one of the questions that is owed to ask is &quot;Is that really what you want?&quot; and, more importantly, &quot;Is that really what the RPG buying audience wants?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T07:07:39-07:00","id":1507055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1506813#post1506813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I note with some trepidation how quickly this moved from &quot;things we'd like to see&quot; to &quot;things I am asking for.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Starting the ball rolling for some possibilities. I don't speak for a collective &quot;we&quot;. I can only say what I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't understand what this is supposed to mean. The Extended Action rules are currently &quot;accumulate this many successes in this many rolls, failing a roll means you need to take a negative Condition to continue, succeeding exceptionally lets you make greater progress or otherwise improve the final result.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Extended actions for long term actions that need to be done in one sitting is lackluster. For instance, you are casting the Sacred Hunt ritual, okay we start are ceremonial dancing *rolls dice*. Did we get enough successes? Nope... *rolls dice*, okay just need 1 more success, *rolls dice*. Extended actions aren't interesting in that context.<br /> <br /> Where I've seen extended actions work well, trying to convince a political rival to be your ally over multiple sessions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The splats that do not have Touchstones are either plain vanilla mortals or operating in a framework where &quot;you have a strong connection to another character&quot; is redundant with something they already have a subsystem for, or else they're Prometheans who don't get guaranteed abiding mortal connections as a splat-level assumption because of what that game is about. </div> </div> </div>Touchstones are an interesting mechanic because they typically link into the Integrity equivalents. Its something that helps facilitate players baking in NPCs into their backstories.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because they are. Because Sin-Eater factions aren't a thing. The splat has had an unmetered global presence for barely more than a hundred years, it's not going to have anything with the institutional weight of the Diamond or the Invictus. </div> </div> </div>Then it'd be interesting to see something like Promethean's lineages or something to give Sin-Eaters an additional character option that matters. Sin-Eater is the only splat where the second biggest character option they pick is a non-option. As far as I can tell your Krewe type doesn't affect anything mechanically<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have that. That's what the Agendas and Tempter associations are about. Lots of demons <i>don't trust Agencies</i> because organized gatherings feel like tempting fate, but the Unchained are generally willing to extend enough trust to interact with other demons on at least a passing basis. </div> </div> </div>Its not made clear in the books. And a lot of issues I have running DtD for new players is them trying to figure out how Demons find other Demons. I love DtD as my first CofD gameline, but that's the biggest issue I have with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not understand what this is supposed to mean. The setting as-presented quietly operates under the assumption that any given chunk of the supernatural is not ubiquitous enough for it to have to be sharing territory with any given other chunk of the supernatural, hence why most of the books that aren't multi-splat focused make little to no reference to other monsters in their sample city sections unless it's a story hook. </div> </div> </div>This problem comes from multiple gamelines written by multiple authors. CofD is a shared universe with shared cosmology, but there are minor issues that can be ironed out like double Arcadia problem or how Mummy Twilight is also a plane of existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not think you have read any of the books these terms come from, because these terms are codified. Dreams are dreams. The Astral is the inside of the soul, which dreams touch the shallows of. The Primordial Dream is the part of the Astral between the soul of humanity as a collective and the soul of the rest of the world; the Horrors of Beasts dwell there. Bastions are the physical structures through which dreams can be accessed, which bleed some of their contents into their surroundings along the Dreaming Roads, which are hidden within the Hedge. </div> </div> </div>There is a lot of confusion with how things are presented in the book. Like if a Changeling, Mage, and Beast enter a person's dream are they all in the same dream? But from how its presented in the books the Changeling would be inside the Bastion, the Mage would be in the Astral, and the Beast would be in the Primordial Dream which is technically the <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?rlz=1C1GCEU_enUS996US996&amp;sxsrf=APwXEddtpdYI4SQ9US5pJC4I0pYetTmvXQ:1680271019964&amp;q=CoD+tenemos&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjHu5WqqYb-AhVUEVkFHXEQCDgQ7xYoAHoECAgQAQ\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>tenemos</i></b></a>\u200b. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Disciplines are built as scaled ladders of monstrosity whose starting powers were explicitly designed to be The Main Thing The Power Does, and they're selectable kit for a splat who can universally make people addicted to them, boost their Physical dicepools, and shrug off being shot multiple times/instantly heal damage it takes multiple days for mortals to heal. Even the Disciplines that aren't clan-specific include free kit like always-on stat boost, psychic invisibility, or making animals do stuff for you.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> A case could be made for putting some space into the Vampire template for starting with a Devotion or two, but Requiem is one of the gamelines where the PCs aren't assumed to be pooling resources on a shared project or serving otherworldly masters or pursuing occult knowledge \u2014 the core vampiric drive is survival as a human-shaped predator-parasite, and Disciplines are very good at that as-is. </div> </div> </div>A few of the splats have two starting character options hidden away in the character creation rules. Starting Werewolves start with Harmony 7 in game, but a First Change Werewolf starts at Harmony 9. Starting Mages start with 6 dots of Arcana, but fresh Mages start with 3 Dots (iirc). Stuff like that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is already the case. </div> </div> </div>For some yes, problem comes up with things like Beast and Mage. Where Beast know every Splat is connected to the Night Mother and for Mage with the Fallen World. I understand Mage has a lot of lore baggage, but there are issues with for instance the Underworld/Hedge/Shadow created from the Fallen World or implied to be. For someone who wants to have the Exarchs, God-Machine, Judges, etc... on a similar power scale its hard to do that when reading the lore makes it seem like the Exarchs created everything. As a Storyteller, I don't like that explanation so I'll remove it from my game, but then I'll have Mage players who get upset because I have to have Supernal Symbology in the Underworld/Spirit/Hedge etc... and then that means it was created by the Exarchs. (It can be exhausting when getting into those debates and my brain just gets fried as a result).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T08:20:08-07:00","id":1507056,"title":"","content":"As others have said, it's more likely that Scion will see more focus instead of a new game being made, especially as OPP seems to be pushing it more than their other properties. You can already hit most of the major urban fantasy archetypes by design, and dedicated books on subjects like its existing vampires and shifters are certainly things OPP can do if they want.<br /> <br /> It won't be a horror game, and it won't be a proper successor to CofD, but that's okay. I'd actually argue Scion is closer to what most groups want to play, it would certainly be for the people I play with if they knew the first thing about mythology (I've literally had to explain who the Olympians are before). Horror is by its nature disempowering, and many people play RPGs for a sense of power (and there's nothing wrong with that, go fangpions).<br /> <br /> Plus honestly I prefer Storypath to Storytelling (and both to Storyteller 5e). Although my personal preferences are more with the crunchier Trinity books than the Scion books, and it's possible that Storypath Ultra will be used for a more CofD-like game (I can certainly see a They Came From... book dedicated to monster hunting shows).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T12:45:14-07:00","id":1507067,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1507055#post1507055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This problem comes from multiple gamelines written by multiple authors. CofD is a shared universe with shared cosmology, but there are minor issues that can be ironed out like double Arcadia problem or how Mummy Twilight is also a plane of existence.</div> </div> </div> </div> Two different Arcadias is a problem? Is this same problem as there being Demons, Unchained, Goetia, Infernal, and the Mummy demons I forget the name of right now all being \u201cdemons\u201d? Heck, some Hobs, Gentry and Changelings probably get in on the fun. And then you have Spirits of Vices. Anyways all I have to say on the matter is thematically Mage Arcadia and Changeling Arcadia are pretty different, with Changeling Arcadia being closer to fairy tale Pandemonium than Mage Arcadia.<br /> <br /> I can however help with this one.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1507055#post1507055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a lot of confusion with how things are presented in the book. Like if a Changeling, Mage, and Beast enter a person's dream are they all in the same dream? But from how its presented in the books the Changeling would be inside the Bastion, the Mage would be in the Astral, and the Beast would be in the Primordial Dream which is technically the <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?rlz=1C1GCEU_enUS996US996&amp;sxsrf=APwXEddtpdYI4SQ9US5pJC4I0pYetTmvXQ:1680271019964&amp;q=CoD+tenemos&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjHu5WqqYb-AhVUEVkFHXEQCDgQ7xYoAHoECAgQAQ\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>tenemos</i></b></a>\u200b.</div> </div> </div> </div> They are, I think you might be confused by their method of travel. Everyone is in the Astral, because Dreams are the Astral shallows. Changelings can just walk there through the dreaming roads. Beast is a little more complicated than the other two, but basically they Primordial Pathways into a resonant Bastion, so someone need to make an ocean or plain or whatever to allow them access. (They can also access the Dreaming Roads, but not every Beast knows they can.) Mages just cast Dream Reaching on their target, and aren\u2019t actually there so much as making a hologram of themselves. They can probably figure out a way to be in person, but the example spell doesn\u2019t really allow it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1507055#post1507055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some yes, problem comes up with things like Beast and Mage. Where Beast know every Splat is connected to the Night Mother and for Mage with the Fallen World. I understand Mage has a lot of lore baggage, but there are issues with for instance the Underworld/Hedge/Shadow created from the Fallen World or implied to be. For someone who wants to have the Exarchs, God-Machine, Judges, etc... on a similar power scale it\u2019s hard to do that when reading the lore makes it seem like the Exarchs created everything. As a Storyteller, I don't like that explanation so I'll remove it from my game, but then I'll have Mage players who get upset because I have to have Supernal Symbology in the Underworld/Spirit/Hedge etc... and then that means it was created by the Exarchs. (It can be exhausting when getting into those debates and my brain just gets fried as a result).</div> </div> </div> </div> I mean\u2026I don\u2019t think it\u2019s a problem? Just because the Exarchs are responsible for the state Fallen World doesn\u2019t mean they made it. It appears they co-opted a lot of pre existing systems, because the big sweeping changes they did make to secure their thrones kinda broke reality, and risked dumping the Fallen World into the Abyss. What they do now is manipulate things so that whatever it does it serves their purpose. They didn\u2019t make the God Machine for example, but they sure do benefit from it, so occasionally they tell Seers to work with it when they think they get more from doing so. Secondly\u2026I think your Mage players might be misunderstanding the concept of Supernal realms. The Underworld isn\u2019t Stygia, the Astral isn\u2019t Pandemonium, and the Hedge isn\u2019t Arcadia. They *might* have links, but that\u2019s more to the Arcanum that they are aligned with than to any Realm. Even the Aether has Death as part of it\u2019s symbol set, for example. It\u2019s equally as valid to say the Underworld has links to the Aether as well as Stygia, because every realm is everywhere. They should be seeing part of their realm every time they open Active Mage Sight, whether they are in Utah, Io, the Shadow reflection of their local bar, or the ship that sails the Final Ocean.<br /> <br /> As for the Dark Mother\u2026it\u2019s literally the collective unconscious\u2019s symbol of Monsterhood/Fear. Yes every splat is connected to it\u2026because they helped shape it and are shaped by it. The Dark Mother is what everyone thinks of when you say monster, because it\u2019s the word \u201cmonster\u201d. When you tell a story about a monster you are speaking of the Dark Mother. And that particular monster, at the same time. Astral stuff gets weird. These gamelines are all about playing monsters, (even hunter), it\u2019s not surprising that they are considered connected to the idea of monsterhood and fear. I\u2019m not a fan how Beast handles depicting that connection, but the premise requires such a connection.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-31-2023, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T15:04:41-07:00","id":1507084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1506995#post1506995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if we're going to ask &quot;Should Onyx Path do it's own version of Chronicles?&quot;, I think one of the questions that is owed to ask is &quot;Is that really what you want?&quot; and, more importantly, &quot;Is that really what the RPG buying audience wants?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit of an unfair question though, because the audience isn't a monolith. I think forums do tend to skew things though. When I play with my normal RPG groups, or even back before COVID and I was a convention regular, there isn't nearly the same level wanting something non-horror. Forums tend to amplify negativity towards the core premise (not just of CofD) because you get a mix of people that like something enough to want part of what is being offered but want to change other bits, and older hands that have played to core conceit enough times to start wondering about tinkering with it for novelty.<br /> <br /> The old &quot;Superheroes with Fangs&quot; thing with VtM when talked about online could make it sound like the vast majority of people only played VtM for the dark power fantasy, but VtM is still a horror game all these decades later, and is still selling despite dark power fantasy games being around if people want that more.<br /> <br /> From a marketing perspective, it doesn't even really matter if some of your customers don't really want a horror game as long as your product is close enough to what they want that they'll buy it and cut out the horror parts.<br /> <br /> The CofD isn't being soft-cancelled because there aren't enough people buying it to be financially viable. Between the people that want it for what it's trying to be, and the people that buy it because it's close enough to what they want that they'll put in the effort to fill in the gaps, it sells as a horror franchise. Hell some percentage of sales are probably just people that buy anything Onyx Path does. From some of the crowdfunding reward tiers that get taken, it's clear there's a few whales in the community.<br /> <br /> I think it's worth thinking about something were the horror is more optional if Onyx Path were to serious consider their own product to replace the profits from making CofD books, but I don't think some reoccurring forum complaints are enough to scrap the horror focus completely by themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T15:31:07-07:00","id":1507085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1507084#post1507084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a bit of an unfair question though, because the audience isn't a monolith. I think forums do tend to skew things though. When I play with my normal RPG groups, or even back before COVID and I was a convention regular, there isn't nearly the same level wanting something non-horror. Forums tend to amplify negativity towards the core premise (not just of CofD) because you get a mix of people that like something enough to want part of what is being offered but want to change other bits, and older hands that have played to core conceit enough times to start wondering about tinkering with it for novelty.<br /> <br /> The old &quot;Superheroes with Fangs&quot; thing with VtM when talked about online could make it sound like the vast majority of people only played VtM for the dark power fantasy, but VtM is still a horror game all these decades later, and is still selling despite dark power fantasy games being around if people want that more.<br /> <br /> From a marketing perspective, it doesn't even really matter if some of your customers don't really want a horror game as long as your product is close enough to what they want that they'll buy it and cut out the horror parts.<br /> <br /> The CofD isn't being soft-cancelled because there aren't enough people buying it to be financially viable. Between the people that want it for what it's trying to be, and the people that buy it because it's close enough to what they want that they'll put in the effort to fill in the gaps, it sells as a horror franchise. Hell some percentage of sales are probably just people that buy anything Onyx Path does. From some of the crowdfunding reward tiers that get taken, it's clear there's a few whales in the community.<br /> <br /> I think it's worth thinking about something were the horror is more optional if Onyx Path were to serious consider their own product to replace the profits from making CofD books, but I don't think some reoccurring forum complaints are enough to scrap the horror focus completely by themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this sensible, even if I find it hard to shake the question (I've been softly asking it since 2015, so some habits die hard).<br /> <br /> Still, to bring it back to my overall point, the idea of OPP doing it's own take on Chronicles(/World) with the serial numbers filed off does still invite a question about core assumptions that might do with a little bit of challenging, and that's more interesting a question that the rehash of &quot;What should a Chronicles 3rd Edition look like&quot; this thread was stealth (&quot;stealth&quot;) going for at any rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T16:09:16-07:00","id":1507087,"title":"","content":"Perhaps an approach to the question that would be most fruitful to dig into: What kind of horror should a potential new product aim for?<br /> <br /> With a mix of pros and cons, the *oD games have gone with an approach of a very vague horror themes in the general setting, and relied on the specifics of each line to highlight specific types of horror more effectively. This stands in contrast to games like CoC, Unknown Armies, and Kult, where even with plenty of character options, the core horror premises are kept more constant across niche play options within the wider games.<br /> <br /> I would personally argue that's one of the big things that makes *oD special and enduring, but it's always left some of the splats feel off kilter. Mage in both has always suffered in it's more subtle &quot;the PCs are supposed to be assholes&quot; style of horror. Exalted also has similar problems. There's nothing else exactly like Exalted, and a lot of people get Exalted even though they really want something else, and the different kinds of Exalted each highlight specific themes and approaches to the concepts of epic heroes. At the same time, some Exalted were pretty dialed in from the start and haven't really had more than mechanical updates, while others have struggled to find their &quot;best&quot; place over multiple editions.<br /> <br /> But it does feel like a lot of contention in the community does stem from the lack of cohesion at a high level of the game with the expectation that individual games will define things more thoroughly. Even with the idea the WoD was &quot;gothic-punk,&quot; and CofD was &quot;gothic,&quot; that really was about Vampire as the other games never seem to feel beholden to those concepts. Exalted does do better here, because even a game of mortals in Creation still holds to the idea of playing heroes in an epic story. What's a high concept like that, which would result in a more thematically unified set of games where what the more subtle or nuanced monsters are easier to interpret because of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T20:56:28-07:00","id":1507094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1507055#post1507055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extended actions for long term actions that need to be done in one sitting is lackluster. For instance, you are casting the Sacred Hunt ritual, okay we start are ceremonial dancing *rolls dice*. Did we get enough successes? Nope... *rolls dice*, okay just need 1 more success, *rolls dice*. Extended actions aren't interesting in that context.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are either moving the goalposts or redefining what &quot;simple&quot; means to something completely unrelated to simplicity for a complaint that could equally unfairly be leveled at any of the other systems that involve multiple rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Touchstones are an interesting mechanic because they typically link into the Integrity equivalents. Its something that helps facilitate players baking in NPCs into their backstories. </div> </div> </div>They also have nothing to do with Cover that isn't already handled by a relationship's value in Cover Experiences, nothing to do with Wisdom that isn't already handled by sympathetic connections and the resolution of the Megalomaniacal Condition, nothing to do with normal Integrity that isn't already handled by the precedent set for protecting loved ones adding a bonus to breaking point rolls, and nothing to do with Pilgrimage at all. If your players need a mechanical incentive to give their characters friends and family, that is not a problem with the game itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then it'd be interesting to see something like Promethean's lineages or something to give Sin-Eaters an additional character option that matters. Sin-Eater is the only splat where the second biggest character option they pick is a non-option. As far as I can tell your Krewe type doesn't affect anything mechanically </div> </div> </div>It affects the three Ceremonies all your krewe members can get for free with Mystery Cult Initiation, which is roughly on par with &quot;you get one free Embed from this category and temporarily get all of them if you go loud&quot; for Incarnation in Demon; their ludonarrative function is to provide a clear general direction for the krewe's mission statement as expressed their choices of Doctrine and Regalia and krewe action.<br /> <br /> Geist is a game full of personal projects that focuses heavily on developing your social connections as a mode of play, and that means <i>building your mystery cult </i>if you want to have depth to the supernaturally-backed group your PCs are a part of. There is no established global society of death-touched half-ghosts to draw on when the Reaper's hungry maw yawns wide below every graveyard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its not made clear in the books. And a lot of issues I have running DtD for new players is them trying to figure out how Demons find other Demons. I love DtD as my first CofD gameline, but that's the biggest issue I have with it. </div> </div> </div>The literal first discussion in the gameline about Agencies, in the corebook, is the third of three short paragraphs about the broad structure of demonic society-such-as-it-is. The <i>first sentence</i> of that paragraph says that the majority of demons view Agencies with suspicion. The next major discussion in the book leads with the statement that most demons don't form rings larger than a handful of their fellows. The list of sample Agencies says outright that most cities don't have Agencies.<br /> <br /> The splat's survivorship bias is described as almost uniformly paranoid, their main means of detecting Aether requires them to spend Aether, and a substantial subset of Falls produce discernible omens in the former angel's surroundings. The rules for investigating a demon to find information that would provoke a compromise if shared with a believing human are in the core and the game's version of the Five Questions for Integrity involve identifying people who might know or suspect you're a demon. Some demons are recruited following psyops persuading them to stop being angels, which makes them about as easy to know about as a freshly Changed werewolf who got bitten for the reason Werewolf typically posits as the explanation for the &quot;a werewolf bite turns you into a werewolf&quot; myth (i.e. a pack recognized the signs of the oncoming Change and got a taste of their blood to make tracking them easier).<br /> <br /> Demons find other demons by <i>paying attention.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a lot of confusion with how things are presented in the book. Like if a Changeling, Mage, and Beast enter a person's dream are they all in the same dream? But from how its presented in the books the Changeling would be inside the Bastion, the Mage would be in the Astral, and the Beast would be in the Primordial Dream which is technically the <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?rlz=1C1GCEU_enUS996US996&amp;sxsrf=APwXEddtpdYI4SQ9US5pJC4I0pYetTmvXQ:1680271019964&amp;q=CoD+tenemos&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjHu5WqqYb-AhVUEVkFHXEQCDgQ7xYoAHoECAgQAQ\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>tenemos</i></b></a>\u200b. </div> </div> </div>I have no idea why you linked to a Google search for the wrong word, but yes, if a changeling enters a Bastion at the same time as a mage and a beast through their respective powers they are in the dream and interact with each other using their respective systems.<br /> <br /> The changeling can leave out of the Bastion that contains the dream on the Dreaming Roads by finding its exit through the oneiromancy systems, the beast is likely interacting with it from a slightly deeper layer in the &quot;Now Playing&quot; part of the personal soul that an individual's active thoughts and dreams play out it (which is nevertheless &quot;in&quot; the dream enough to interact with the changeling) and will probably want to get out of them by the end of the scene for analogous reasons to the changeling not wanting to get dumped into a random spot in the universe, and the mage is almost certainly just using the spell that projects you into somebody's dreams. If the beast opens a Primordial Pathway to their Lair to merge with their Horror, the dream will be spacially overlapped with a Chamber in the Primordial Dream, and anyone attempting to leave that Chamber will find themselves smack dab in the middle of the Astral, but that's leaving the dream just as surely as the changeling stepping out onto the Dreaming Roads or the mage ending their spell.<br /> <br /> The Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle, the book where a bunch of crossover advice and notes are included (where there isn't already material in another book to direct to), explicitly says how Bastions interact with other dream-handling abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A few of the splats have two starting character options hidden away in the character creation rules. Starting Werewolves start with Harmony 7 in game, but a First Change Werewolf starts at Harmony 9. Starting Mages start with 6 dots of Arcana, but fresh Mages start with 3 Dots (iirc). Stuff like that. </div> </div> </div>And your contention here is that you think the Kindred template is somehow analogous to the latter options because there are fewer dots, despite the options for those dots including ritual sorcery Disciplines whose covenants take murderous pains to keep them proprietary?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For some yes, problem comes up with things like Beast and Mage. Where Beast know every Splat is connected to the Night Mother and for Mage with the Fallen World. I understand Mage has a lot of lore baggage, but there are issues with for instance the Underworld/Hedge/Shadow created from the Fallen World or implied to be. For someone who wants to have the Exarchs, God-Machine, Judges, etc... on a similar power scale its hard to do that when reading the lore makes it seem like the Exarchs created everything. As a Storyteller, I don't like that explanation so I'll remove it from my game, but then I'll have Mage players who get upset because I have to have Supernal Symbology in the Underworld/Spirit/Hedge etc... and then that means it was created by the Exarchs. (It can be exhausting when getting into those debates and my brain just gets fried as a result). </div> </div> </div>You do understand the function of mythology, right? Like, the things that are objectively true about the setting are largely in the present:<br /> <br /> The Supernal describes the Phenomenal (imperfectly, thanks to the Abyss, and, as Dave pointed out so many years ago, the Forces Arcanum describing electricity doesn't mean electricity is made of magic) and the Exarchs rule the Supernal through their subjugation of many of its remaining denizens.<br /> <br /> The Begotten have a metaphysical connection with the vast majority of supernatural creatures (when they get their powers from being merges with a supernatural being from the &quot;conceptual being who resonates with things to do with that concept&quot; category).<br /> <br /> The Arisen were made through the Rite of Return and are supported by cults to the Judges (and the rest of their history is for them to find out at their peril)<br /> <br /> Werewolves are not-quite-Flesh and not-quite-Spirit and have drives to hunt and maintain territory that have always led many of them to interpret other supernatural creatures through a lens that lets them justify acting as though they're something Uratha should deal with (for which Sin-Eaters and Storm Lords will probably always have some rocky ground to cross in meeting).<br /> <br /> Demons and changelings have big divine monsters after them, the fears and hopes around which lead many of them to interpret other supernatural creatures as being related to those god-monsters as additional threats to be tackled or avoided or as vectors for aid to be courted or exploited (if not both).<br /> <br /> Hunters who haven't managed to catch enough of a break to go into &quot;remission&quot; have a chasing-the-supernatural problem, and vampires have sires and Prometheans have genitors and deviants have progenitors (or at least circumstances that made them what they are), and so on.<br /> <br /> If your players are demanding &quot;Supernal Symbology&quot; in the Phenomenal otherworlds they're asking for nonsense, but also the analogous phenomena there are to be found in the Incarnae and Celestines of the Shadow, the tableaus of the Underworld's Lower Mysteries, powerful and deeply hidden facilities, and the depths of Arcadia and Duat. Secret-levers-of-the-world stuff has gotten more PC-accessible in 2e<br /> <br /> The big &quot;imperial powers&quot; of the setting that aren't the God-Machine are operating from a long way away through the finite assets of related supernatural creatures, agents, and real estate, and the God-Machine is explicitly powerful locally on the strength of lots of little operations going well in a way that creates a durable power base that nevertheless relies on processes with weak points PCs in a game of Demon can target, and for that and other reasons even the Machine tends to operate at a remove by favoring the mundane approach if the occult isn't required. Everything can be kept separate from each other or have excuses made for their interaction, it's just that Mage and Beast are specifically lines about exploring the supernatural and learning about supernatural creatures and so their toolkits facilitate that and their in-character mythology supports them engaging in those pursuits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T17:59:29-07:00","id":1507523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1507084#post1507084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a bit of an unfair question though, because the audience isn't a monolith. I think forums do tend to skew things though. When I play with my normal RPG groups, or even back before COVID and I was a convention regular, there isn't nearly the same level wanting something non-horror. Forums tend to amplify negativity towards the core premise (not just of CofD) because you get a mix of people that like something enough to want part of what is being offered but want to change other bits, and older hands that have played to core conceit enough times to start wondering about tinkering with it for novelty.<br /> <br /> The old &quot;Superheroes with Fangs&quot; thing with VtM when talked about online could make it sound like the vast majority of people only played VtM for the dark power fantasy, but VtM is still a horror game all these decades later, and is still selling despite dark power fantasy games being around if people want that more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the horror/superheroes with fangs dichotomy is a false one. A big part of the appeal to me is the most obvious one: you get to be the monster. You get to do things that are horrifying, but you don't necessarily experience the horror as you would in other &quot;horror&quot; media since your character is often the source of it. I think this is actually quite unique, even when other RPGs let you play as a &quot;monster&quot; they often make it so that you are really just playing a hero wearing a monster outfit.<br /> <br /> This also affects the social dynamics around the table in interesting ways. Legend of the Five Rings can be just as political a game as Vampire, if not even more so. However players don't expect the other players to backstab them at the first opportunity in L5R (at least not at my table), and they don't fondly reminisce about the time one player character betrayed and diablerised another. Other CofD games don't necessarily have this element, but most of them do share the feature that awful things are going to be done by your character and happen to your character over the course of the game. I might expect my packmates in Werewolf to have my back, but I don't expect them to act in a way that would be considered <i>moral </i>(except by other Werewolves). Exploring the odd needs of these characters, how they square these realities with their human moralities, or exploring the odd blue-orange moralities that they end up adopting instead are all compelling pieces of these games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T22:56:18-07:00","id":1507554,"title":"","content":"I feel like this is basically asking for a 3e with one tweaked core rule, every splat being based on a central template, and a lore book with authoritative answers to all the shared-cosmology lore questions that have ever come up? Am I missing something? What are we supposed to be pitching?<br /> <br /> Because I want quaternions. That's my request. If you rotate a vampire along the correctly chosen axis in N-fantastical space, you should get a promethean. Their integrity equivalents are just two parts of the same number line anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T01:02:42-07:00","id":1507561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1506790#post1506790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, they kinda already have via Scion 2e. Trinity 2e isn't hard to give a more urban fantasy edge instead of a speculative fiction edge if you want to do so.<br /> <br /> Given Trinity 2e a supplement along the lines of JL: Dark or the Midnight Suns (which mixes the default superhero settings of DC and Marvel with more fantasy aspects) so it's not overtly competing with CofD or WoD, and I think a lot of people would be happy as it wouldn't be hard to use that to replicated WoD or CofD with those tools.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Trinity 2E</b> is <b><i>already</i></b> going by <b>CofD</b> tropes in it. In supplements we got:<ul><li><b>TC Assassin</b> - that works very much like secret societies books of <b>CoD</b>. Even more, they work more or less '<b>Guardians of the Veil</b>-type' book.</li> <li><b>Trinity Player's Guide</b> ( <a href=\"https://www.backerkit.com/c/onyx-path/trinity-continuum-player-s-guide#top\" target=\"_blank\">now in crowdfunding</a> ) - Have alternate dimensions, time travels, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1505101-astral-space-in-trinity-continuum\">astral realms</a>, even planetary jumping. ( Whole of <b>Mage</b>, <b>Changeling</b> and <b>Beast </b>fans should be content. )</li> <li><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488826-tc-2e-magic-in-aether-and-adventure-%F0%9F%98%B2\"><b>'Magic' in Adventure, Aether, Aegis and before</b></a> - I make quotations as it's 'super science in disguise' - but, in reality, most of Inspired stuff and Super Science in <b>Trinity</b> is much more magic than proper sciense. <b>Magic in TC</b> is really <i>'if it looks like a duck, swims like a duck, and quacks like a duck, then it probably is a duck.' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </i>I run now both low fantasy <b>Scion</b> game ( Iron Levels ) and <b>Trinity Continuum</b> ones - and TC is much more in feel of CoD than ever - simply how it's constructed.</li> <li><b>Trinity</b> even now have official Victorian era monsters in from <b>Aether </b>- with coming <b>Aethernaut Collection</b> we will have things like official (Castlevania style) Dracula, Frankenstein Monster, Invisible Man, etc.</li> <li>For fans of <b>Dark Eras</b> - <b>Trinity</b> as whole basically Dark Eras 3.0, with Adventure, Aether, Aeon ( futuristic ) and Anima an Aegis in works.</li> </ul>In conclusion - If you want to run 'dark/light urban fantasy' game now - <b>Trinity Continuum</b> is your choosing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You only do not have complex systems to play vampire, werewolves, mummies, etc. ( But can work easier/simpler ones with ease. ) You even HAVE now sorcerers to play in form of mesmerists. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-06-2023, 04:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T01:15:50-07:00","id":1507562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1507561#post1507561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Trinity 2E</b> is <b><i>already</i></b> going by <b>CofD</b> tropes in it. In supplements we got:<ul><li><b>TC Assassin</b> - that works very much like secret societies books of <b>CoD</b>. Even more, they work more or less '<b>Guardians of the Veil</b>-type' book.</li> <li><b>Trinity Player's Guide</b> ( <a href=\"https://www.backerkit.com/c/onyx-path/trinity-continuum-player-s-guide#top\" target=\"_blank\">now in crowdfunding</a> ) - Have alternate dimensions, time travels, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1505101-astral-space-in-trinity-continuum\">astral realms</a>, even planetary jumping. ( Whole of <b>Mage</b>, <b>Changeling</b> and <b>Beast </b>fans should be content. )</li> <li><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488826-tc-2e-magic-in-aether-and-adventure-%F0%9F%98%B2\"><b>'Magic' in Adventure, Aether, Aegis and before</b></a> - I make quotations as it's 'super science in disguise' - but, in reality, most of Inspired stuff and Super Science in <b>Trinity</b> is much more magic than proper sciense. <b>Magic in TC</b> is really <i>'if it looks like a duck, swims like a duck, and quacks like a duck, then it probably is a duck.' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </i>I run now both low fantasy <b>Scion</b> game ( Iron Levels ) and <b>Trinity Continuum</b> ones - and TC is much more in feel of CoD than ever - simply how it's constructed.</li> <li><b>Trinity</b> even now have official Victorian era monsters in from <b>Aether </b>- with coming <b>Aethernaut Collection</b> we will have things like official (Castlevania style) Dracula, Frankenstein Monster, Invisible Man, etc.</li> <li>For fans of <b>Dark Eras</b> - <b>Trinity</b> as whole basically Dark Eras 3.0, with Adventure, Aether, Aeon ( futuristic ) and Anima an Aegis in works.</li> </ul>In conclusion - If you want to run 'dark/light urban fantasy' game now - <b>Trinity Continuum</b> is your choosing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You only do not have complex systems to play vampire, werewolves, mummies, etc. ( But can work easier/simpler ones with ease. ) You even HAVE now sorcerers to play in form of mesmerists. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Trinity scratches the itch for Trinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T04:09:07-07:00","id":1507573,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Trinity 2e is certainly building up the tools one would need to to a fan-hack of CofD games in the Storypath system. That doesn't mean the official books are what CofD fans actually want, or even what broader urban fantasy fans want. It's like looking at a Lego boat, and thinking about how it wouldn't be that hard to ignore the &quot;boat&quot; instructions and make a spaceship; esp. if you buy a few other kits too. You can do it, sure, but you could also just buy the Lego spaceship kit instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T07:03:02-07:00","id":1507581,"title":"","content":"Having played a couple of Storypath games - a campaign of Scion and a few one shots of They Came From Beyond the Grave - I'm much less convinced that the port of CofD material to Storypath is either easy or worthwhile. To actually get any benefit you would largely have to reinvent the same material again. I can't speak for other fans, but what I want is not vaguely horror themed supplements tacked-on to Scion or Trinity, what I want is more CofD, especially Requiem and Forsaken. I've followed Trinity and Scion with diminishing enthusiasm and now I'm pretty sure that they just aren't the games for me.<br /> <br /> They Came From is a much more positive experience, but I actually feel it is held back by the Storypath system rather than enabled by it, and would be more enjoyable if the whole thing could be reduced to quips, stunts, and cinematics. In any case, They Came From scratches a very different itch to CofD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T11:31:33-07:00","id":1507594,"title":"","content":"Pretty interesting thread - I've personally appreciated the thinking being expressed here. One thing though, which addresses the title of this thread if not the rest of the OP itself, is the unalterable fact that Paradox owns both WoD and CofD. We don't, so if we were to create a new urban horror or fantasy game line, we wouldn't be able to basically do the new edition of any of the games under those two brands. We wouldn't be able to have a group of vampires called the Grujah (or even the Malkovians!) who are real hot tempered, or a magic-using group called the Beers of the Throne. So anything we'd be creating would have to be something new. Which is not to say that we couldn't explore the same or similar themes, structure the game world in ways that we know work for horror gaming, or use every bit of the experience we've gained after decades of creating WoD and CofD projects, not to mention learning from creating those new projects where we have come close to horror - as some folks have mentioned up-thread.<br /> <br /> As for system design, we wouldn't be using yet another version of the old WW systems, we'd use our own game system: the Storypath System. In fact, I'd imagine we'd use something like Storypath Ultra, the newest iteration that we'll be previewing at the GAMA Trade Show at the end of the month, and that folks are seeing hints of in the World Below teaser blog these last bunch of weeks. The World Below uses Storypath Ultra, and while it is a fantasy game, it is pretty dark (no pun intended with the setting being underground) and we're learning a lot about how Ultra delivers gaming that allows the system to complement the setting.<br /> <br /> Anyway, hope I haven't derailed the conversation, just wanted to illustrate some of the realities we face if, sometime in the dim mists of the future, we went ahead and got back on that horrific horse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T16:04:40-07:00","id":1507618,"title":"","content":"Looking at the recent previews for The World Below, it does seem a closer fit to WoD and CoD.<br /> <br /> Not TC and Scion. (Well, maybe sans Mythos and Dragon.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T17:11:28-07:00","id":1507627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1507618#post1507618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the recent previews for The World Below, it does seem a closer fit to WoD and CoD.<br /> <br /> Not TC and Scion. (Well, maybe sans Mythos and Dragon.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we reading the same previews?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T17:13:12-07:00","id":1507628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1507627#post1507627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are we reading the same previews?</div> </div> </div> </div>The two Callings and the Umbral Wisdom?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T17:15:08-07:00","id":1507629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1507628#post1507628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The two Callings and the Umbral Wisdom?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The take I'm getting from that is more dark post-apocalyptic fantasy than urban horror/fantasy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If I were going to posit something World/Chronicles adjacent that might also point a way a new one from OPP might go, I might point at <a href=\"http://www.nahualrpg.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Nahaul</a>-start the setting going a logical step in the progression to where the supernatural is in a semi-open state-people know of it, and you could, in fact, find your way to a fairy law office or an angel butcher shop, but it's small enough of a niche that you much of the world still looks the same, unless you have a particular reason to walk in particular neighborhoods at particular times. You know the taco truck that comes by on Tuesday is a cheaper alternative than healthcare, and maybe you just don't ask why that is. Or maybe you know, and the taboo is half the point.<br /> <br /> Arguably, it has more of the flavor of -of Darkness games than some of the other suggestions so far, but it's a take on the genre that the -of Darkness games hasn't used as it's baked-in setting assumption.<br /> <br /> (Why not those vampire stories from about a decade where vampries more formally join society or rebel against it? That's a little <i>too</i> open for my tastes.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-06-2023, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts