 by on Tuesday is a cheaper alternative than healthcare, and maybe you just don't ask why that is. Or maybe you know, and the taboo is half the point.<br /> <br /> Arguably, it has more of the flavor of -of Darkness games than some of the other suggestions so far, but it's a take on the genre that the -of Darkness games hasn't used as it's baked-in setting assumption.<br /> <br /> (Why not those vampire stories from about a decade where vampries more formally join society or rebel against it? That's a little <i>too</i> open for my tastes.) </div> </div> </div>Huh, that game looks interesting\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T18:25:19-07:00","id":1507637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1507636#post1507636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh indeed \u2014 it\u2019s likely not even \u2018more Dark Post-Apocalypse\u2019, and just that flat-out. I only meant what I said in a comparative sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Huh, that game looks interesting\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really good, I would recommend it, particularly if you are a fan of PbtA and FitD games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T20:43:14-07:00","id":1507646,"title":"","content":"If I, for whatever reason, had to pitch an urban fantasy game that hit some of the same tastes as the urban horror of the WoD/CoD gamelines, but was distinct, I think my starting point would be assuming something similar to Mirrors' Woundgate alternate setting as the default, and reworking the general design of the games from there. The various supernaturals would possibly interact with each other more in their passages between this world and the shard worlds, so maybe present the game with an assumption of different supernatural types sharing a party more regularly than the WoD/CoD games assume. Presenting in game system terms as more like X-splat=supernatural type, Y-splat=political or philosophical factions that are shared across supernaturals instead of unique to each, and Z-splat=current X-splat, Clan, Seeming, and so forth, would make for a game less suited to tackling the unique horrors encapsulated by each game as it stands, but more suited to action-oriented urban fantasy with many different supernatural creatures appearing in the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27841-haintbleu","name":"HaintBleu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T21:17:18-07:00","id":1507650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaintBleu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1507646#post1507646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presenting in game system terms as more like X-splat=supernatural type, Y-splat=political or philosophical factions that are shared across supernaturals instead of unique to each, and Z-splat=current X-splat, Clan, Seeming, and so forth, would make for a game less suited to tackling the unique horrors encapsulated by each game as it stands, but more suited to action-oriented urban fantasy with many different supernatural creatures appearing in the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>... which seems what Scion 2E is <b><i>already</i></b> doing on Denizens area - just lookis on offficial Denizes write-ups and their Paths changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T22:26:15-07:00","id":1507657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1507650#post1507650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... which seems what Scion 2E is <b><i>already</i></b> doing on Denizens area - just lookis on offficial Denizes write-ups and their Paths changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every game has stories it's best at telling, characters that only make sense in that setting. For example, the Silver Ladder only makes sense in the terms of the gnostic setting of Mage the Awakening. You can have a call back to them in other systems, but those characters wouldn't make much sense in Scion. Even if it has some of the same themes, I don't feel that Scion should be advertised as a Chronicles alike, it would be doing it a disservice. It wasn't built to be Chronicles, it was made to be Scion. It should focus on what Scion does best, not to be trying to be a replacement for Chronicles. I mean, I could hypothetically use DnD for Mage. I could! But should I? DnD mages aren't the Awakened, their rules and lore have next to no resemblance to Awakening. I just don't think it would be as enjoyable an experience for people seeking an Awakening game. If Onyx Path does make its own new line focusing on being a spiritual successor to Chronicles, I would be happy with that. If they took what they learned, and made something new that was almost unrecognizable, I would be content with that. But I don't think they should try to twist their other games into being Chronicles. That's not fair to anyone. If they want to explore some of the same themes and concepts, sure why not. But it should come from that particular game lines perspective, not the Chronicle's one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T01:22:44-07:00","id":1507674,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's what wyrdhamster was trying to say. I think the point was just that the setup HaintBleu proposed is already how Scion 2e uses the Storypath Paths traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T13:14:04-07:00","id":1507709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1507674#post1507674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's what wyrdhamster was trying to say. I think the point was just that the setup HaintBleu proposed is already how Scion 2e uses the Storypath Paths traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that\u2019s the case, sorry Wyrd. I must have misunderstood your intentions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T21:24:16-07:00","id":1507736,"title":"","content":"Yeah - I pointed that mechanically speaking, Scion 2E already doing more or less what you want. BUT it's limited to Scion verse. I, as fan material, just use the engine to emulate CoD beings in Scion verse. But it's totally UNOFFICIAL one. OPP sticking things separately between CoD and Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-08-2023, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T21:20:40-07:00","id":1509347,"title":"","content":"If Onyxpath were to write a new Urban Fantasy there was this post on monday meeting notes that I agree with this to an extent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hiram<br /> If you were to create a new Urban Fantasy line, there are lots of things I\u2019d expect of it:<br /> <br /> * First of all is to have the queerest developer and writers working on it.<br /> <br /> * I would like it to be written with an even more leftist perspective than the CofD was/is.<br /> <br /> * This game line would have to do away with most if not all WoD trappings. No \u201cclans\u201d or Werewolf \u201ctribes\u201d or reused names except maybe 1 or 2 that can\u2019t be helped (like nosferatu).<br /> <br /> * Ideally it should be either 1 game containing all of these supernaturals and their sub-mechanics while having an underlying common theme to all<br /> OR<br /> very distinct mechanics to reflect each line\u2019s themes (and no crossover compatibility at all due to it).<br /> The latter would produce the best and most consistent games in terms of communicating their proposed experience. </div> </div> </div>As for Scion I do mask of mythos (Cthulhu supplement) sort of hits some of the beats and I know some people consider the playable dragons to be considered more cofd/wod than scion.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T08:45:28-07:00","id":1509478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509347#post1509347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Onyxpath were to write a new Urban Fantasy there was this post on monday meeting notes that I agree with this to an extent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for Scion I do mask of mythos (Cthulhu supplement) sort of hits some of the beats and I know some people consider the playable dragons to be considered more cofd/wod than scion.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree heavily with the first two, because that limits the perspectives being shown and drawn from. Urban fantasy and game development works best with a broad range of experiences being drawn from, even those you may not find match your own. It also restricts your available writers - and it limits the spread of people who can easily access it. <br /> <br /> More on the topic, there's really two approaches that an Urban Fantasy setting can take:<br /> 1) Our world and the supernatural world have always been/recently have been integrated with one another. You have a vampire working for the dmv etc. Think Shadowrun as an idea for what you can do.<br /> 2) Our world and the supernatural world have a strict delineation between the two. This is more of the classic world of darkness/chronicles of darkness feel, with the supernatural tucked away behind what would be considered normal.<br /> <br /> A way to do a deliberate break with CoD/WoD would be to adopt the first, but that leads to a very different feel to the setting. There's a lot of groundwork that will need to be done in both scenarios, in order to get a concrete mood and themes with the setting that has internal logical consistency. Still, certain things can be taken in terms of what it SHOULD bring if it wants to lean more into the horror-punk aesthetic of CoD, along with being a good roleplaying setting.<br /> <br /> 1) (Almost) Everything is a matter of perspective. One person's demon is another's angel or god or whatever. Nobody is seeing the whole elephant of the supernatural. <br /> 2) Antagonist factions to your default player group have a point that is hard to refute, even if they're extremists about it. <br /> 3) Being inhuman matters. Vampires can be polite and happy people, but in the end they will happily drink your blood and justify their own behaviors. They aren't human, even if they're trying their best to be so.<br /> 4) Being human matters. Wizards and psychics need to have some sort of contrast with other supernaturals, but also humans. Believing themselves the best of all humanity or as a step away from being inhuman creates contrasts with both baseline mortal people and the supernatural. Similarly, a vampire fighting to not start seeing people as just prey should be a factor. Even baseline humans can act like something inhuman<br /> 5) Sometimes you just can't win. Your player characters are sometimes in a doomed situation and whatever they struggle for, it is unlikely to be fully accomplished. But there's still more than a few reasons to fight back, and small victories are still victories. <br /> 6) Mechanical distinctions are important but complete stand alone entities hurt a unified setting. No man is an island and no inhuman supernatural is going to be totally isolated from whatever else is going bump in the night. Being focused on their own problems is fine, but there should be reasons for them to stretch out to other spooky things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T10:27:57-07:00","id":1509490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arch-Magos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509478#post1509478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) (Almost) Everything is a matter of perspective. One person's demon is another's angel or god or whatever. Nobody is seeing the whole elephant of the supernatural.<br /> 2) Antagonist factions to your default player group have a point that is hard to refute, even if they're extremists about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ack, no. This is one of those things that Chronicles has been really good about- it's moral gray conflicts stand all out all the more starkly because there are people who are completely in the wrong, and the game doesn't shy away from the fact that a lot of shit that happens come from people who just don't care about the people, places, and ideas they damage in pursuit of their own desire and hunger, and making it clear how that mirrors real world issues to allow exploration of it. It's good horror with a purpose in that way, which is a general hallmark of these games on the whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T10:42:37-07:00","id":1509493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509490#post1509490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ack, no. This is one of those things that Chronicles has been really good about- it's moral gray conflicts stand all out all the more starkly because there are people who are completely in the wrong, and the game doesn't shy away from the fact that a lot of shit that happens come from people who just don't care about the people, places, and ideas they damage in pursuit of their own desire and hunger, and making it clear how that mirrors real world issues to allow exploration of it. It's good horror with a purpose in that way, which is a general hallmark of these games on the whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean by the first is that there's no true right answer to what makes the world actually tick. Good horror keeps things under wraps and explains what it needs to, in my opinion. When something breaks your rules, there should be a good reason as to why it does though. <br /> <br /> I do stand by the primary antagonists within your group having a point to them as a rule. The Seers and the Pure are both better antagonists when you can understand why they hold their perspective and both have something of a point - the Exarchs have pretty much already won so why fight them in the case of the Seers. Vampire really doesn't have a primary antagonist 'faction' in opposition to the covenants (I guess VII, but VII is pretty flexible in what it is), but each covenant effectively acts as an antagonist to the others. Changeling has the Privateers/Loyalists, Prometheans don't really have this but don't need it really same with Mummies, Sin-Eaters have the Kerberoi, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T10:46:33-07:00","id":1509494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arch-Magos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509493#post1509493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I mean by the first is that there's no true right answer to what makes the world actually tick. Good horror keeps things under wraps and explains what it needs to, in my opinion. When something breaks your rules, there should be a good reason as to why it does though.<br /> <br /> I do stand by the primary antagonists within your group having a point to them as a rule. The Seers and the Pure are both better antagonists when you can understand why they hold their perspective and both have something of a point - the Exarchs have pretty much already won so why fight them in the case of the Seers. Vampire really doesn't have a primary antagonist 'faction' in opposition to the covenants (I guess VII, but VII is pretty flexible in what it is), but each covenant effectively acts as an antagonist to the others. Changeling has the Privateers/Loyalists, Prometheans don't really have this but don't need it really same with Mummies, Sin-Eaters have the Kerberoi, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see what you mean and can agree to it.<br /> <br /> (Not that it matters, but Vampires have Belial's Brood, the Arisen have the Shuankhsen and Deceived, and Sin-Eater's are more directly opposed by Reapers. Promethean's ARE countered by the Centimani, but the Centimani have always been portrayed with a wider range than their contemporaries.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T10:48:59-07:00","id":1509495,"title":"","content":"The WoD really demonstrated how much overdoing the &quot;everything is relative and shares off grey,&quot; can end up muddying the water more than making the games more fun to play. It's good to have antagonists that are darker hues and all, but a large interconnected supernatural horror game needs some solid black in there.<br /> <br /> It's also creates a lot of uncomfortable thing when you try to always make the bad guys sympathetic. The trying to make factions like the Black Spiral Dancers into &quot;having a point, but they're just a bit extreme about it,&quot; sounds really bad when their tactics include torture, sexual violence, mass murder, and so on. I don't think a lot of people actually want to play in a setting where there's some &quot;hard to refute point&quot; being made by those sorts of actions. If your side thinks those are valid tactics, your side doesn't have a hard to refuse point, the means refute it easily.<br /> <br /> So either you cut out the worst of the worst... and the setting is less horrific and less dark... or you end up making the setting really squicky because it validates horrific things.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Since I'm a bit slow on the typing:<br /> <br /> Rather than &quot;primary&quot; antagonist, I think the important distinction is whether or not the antagonists are meant to be philosophic ones or not. If the game needs a strong philosophic foil (Pentacle vs. the Seers), sure, the Seers need to have a point. If the game doesn't so much, you can safely use other types of conflicts (The Pure and The Bale Hounds really don't need to have a point; even if The Pure might sorta have a point, their actions clearly fall into the auto-refutation category).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 04-24-2023, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T10:49:55-07:00","id":1509496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arch-Magos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509493#post1509493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans don't really have this</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemists/ Centimani. Different perspectives on Humanity, and thus the validity of Transhumanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T11:03:33-07:00","id":1509499,"title":"","content":"Well, Alchemists, like Heroes, run afoul a bit of He Who's Name Shall Be Remembered as a Curse doing the whole, &quot;this book only deals with the really horrible ones, in theory there's greater moral variety, but the ones with a point aren't what the game is about so we're not going to discuss their existence further,&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T11:08:21-07:00","id":1509500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509495#post1509495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The WoD really demonstrated how much overdoing the &quot;everything is relative and shares off grey,&quot; can end up muddying the water more than making the games more fun to play. It's good to have antagonists that are darker hues and all, but a large interconnected supernatural horror game needs some solid black in there.<br /> <br /> It's also creates a lot of uncomfortable thing when you try to always make the bad guys sympathetic. The trying to make factions like the Black Spiral Dancers into &quot;having a point, but they're just a bit extreme about it,&quot; sounds really bad when their tactics include torture, sexual violence, mass murder, and so on. I don't think a lot of people actually want to play in a setting where there's some &quot;hard to refute point&quot; being made by those sorts of actions. If your side thinks those are valid tactics, your side doesn't have a hard to refuse point, the means refute it easily.<br /> <br /> So either you cut out the worst of the worst... and the setting is less horrific and less dark... or you end up making the setting really squicky because it validates horrific things.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Since I'm a bit slow on the typing:<br /> <br /> Rather than &quot;primary&quot; antagonist, I think the important distinction is whether or not the antagonists are meant to be philosophic ones or not. If the game needs a strong philosophic foil (Pentacle vs. the Seers), sure, the Seers need to have a point. If the game doesn't so much, you can safely use other types of conflicts (The Pure and The Bale Hounds really don't need to have a point; even if The Pure might sorta have a point, their actions clearly fall into the auto-refutation category).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I kinda mean that it's good to have a philosophical antagonist in some form for a horror game line. It isn't needed for some but I think they do add something special. Refuting their point doesn't necessarily need to be hard but if you're plainly playing a monster, having your antagonist group doing monstrous things with a similar justification to your own helps ram that point home that you're in character jumping through hoops to justify yourself. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509494#post1509494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I see what you mean and can agree to it.<br /> <br /> (Not that it matters, but Vampires have Belial's Brood, the Arisen have the Shuankhsen and Deceived, and Sin-Eater's are more directly opposed by Reapers. Promethean's ARE countered by the Centimani, but the Centimani have always been portrayed with a wider range than their contemporaries.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Reapers slipped my mind, thanks for the reminder.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509496#post1509496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemists/ Centimani. Different perspectives on Humanity, and thus the validity of Transhumanism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same with the Centimani, I was considering alchemists more the Promethean foil but they didn't quite fit - neither really are humans seeking to become inhuman and rejecting humanity. Centimani can ask the question of 'why become human' pretty well though, same as Alchemists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T12:15:21-07:00","id":1509511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arch-Magos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509500#post1509500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I kinda mean that it's good to have a philosophical antagonist in some form for a horror game line. It isn't needed for some but I think they do add something special. Refuting their point doesn't necessarily need to be hard but if you're plainly playing a monster, having your antagonist group doing monstrous things with a similar justification to your own helps ram that point home that you're in character jumping through hoops to justify yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019d prefer it if most had a good philosophical villain. Like, not every game needs to be deep, but I\u2019d like depth and nuance to be explorable in setting. For example, I don\u2019t begrudge anyone running the Abyss and it\u2019s servants as always chaotic evil dnd monsters, but I think it would be a much more fun antagonist to a group trying to improve the Fallen World with a Scelestus earnestly trying to do the same thing through the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T13:10:30-07:00","id":1509514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> eh no. Mummy is great for this as the Shuankshen are both the soul chewed horrors of the goddess of entropy who threatened to eat the universe but also the sacrificed slaves of the Nameless Empire who do have a good reason to be pissed and the Deceived are both the victimized mummies stuck with a shard of an insanely godling stuck in them and the pissed off insane shard of a Shan iatu who wants revenge against the other Shan iatu because their double cross was double crossed.<br /> <br /> Mummy antagonists straddle a great line between getting their side of things but also being horrible monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I'm not as familiar with mummy as other game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T13:52:10-07:00","id":1509520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks. It's easily my favourite game line and I think it and Werewolf have some of the coolest antagonist. Be cool if Paradox got out of the way so we can get a Night Horrors book.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're too busy letting swedish larpers try and fail to do classic WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T15:16:50-07:00","id":1509527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arch-Magos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509520#post1509520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're too busy letting swedish larpers try and fail to do classic WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly is going on with that side of the fence? I mostly see people upset for this or that change, but why are the various 5th editions so different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T15:31:50-07:00","id":1509528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509527#post1509527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What exactly is going on with that side of the fence? I mostly see people upset for this or that change, but why are the various 5th editions so different?</div> </div> </div> </div>The various details are numerous, but the broad trends can almost laughably come down to how very clear it is that Paradox wanted to make Chronicle games but with the brand appeal of World and had either no ideas on how to actually implement that or terrible ideas on how to implement that. Details can be found a plenty in the World of Darkness threads.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I think the best encapsulation of the entire thing is that The Imbued don't exist in Hunter: the Reckoning 5E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-24-2023, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T15:44:13-07:00","id":1509530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509527#post1509527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What exactly is going on with that side of the fence? I mostly see people upset for this or that change, but why are the various 5th editions so different?</div> </div> </div> </div>For H5 and W5 it comes down to Justin Achilli preferring the extremes of 'street level' play, as well as having a 'less rules=more narrative' view. For V5 I think it's a mixture of leaning into what the designers had been playing for the previous half decade, but there's also a noticeable attempt to appeal to left leaning 20-somethings. And to clarify that's European Left, not US Left. Which leads to stuff like the Camarilla deposing the Sabbat as default enemies, the splintering of the Tremere, and the rise of the Anarchs (who have nabbed some of the Sabbath's qualities).<br /> <br /> There's also discontent over the reboot nature (soft for V5, hard for everything else). Reboots certainly aren't bad, honestly VtM probably needed one just to make it easier to get into, but they are going to piss off anybody into the old lore. Which is bad when WoD's selling point is the lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T06:05:26-07:00","id":1509577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509528#post1509528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The various details are numerous, but the broad trends can almost laughably come down to how very clear it is that Paradox wanted to make Chronicle games but with the brand appeal of World and had either no ideas on how to actually implement that or terrible ideas on how to implement that. Details can be found a plenty in the World of Darkness threads.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I think the best encapsulation of the entire thing is that The Imbued don't exist in Hunter: the Reckoning 5E.</div> </div> </div> </div>H5's essentially a Vigil 1e clone, except without the additional things and system of Vigil that made it worth playing. There's some absolutely braindead fluff in there too, like retconning most of the Orpheus gameline (why) and there's essentially zero reason to play H5 when Vigil or Hunters Hunted exists. Hunter getting a new edition before Mage, Werewolf, or even Wraith is also mindboggling. My only guess is they knew Chronicles was getting Vigil 2e release and slapped together a game in a short time based on that because someone in PDX watched the Mori hololive Vigil game as they had to sign off on it happening because of vtuber agency policies to avoid lawsuits. It's really beyond me why they did this. Werewolf 5e is already looking like a dumpster fire and I can't wait for the shitshow explosion as mage fans find out about their 5e - Ascension fans are a whole different breed of dedicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T08:40:49-07:00","id":1509587,"title":"","content":"Wow. Just wow. I can completely understand the anger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arch-Magos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509577#post1509577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because someone in PDX watched the Mori hololive Vigil game as they had to sign off on it happening because of vtuber agency policies to avoid lawsuits.</div> </div> </div> </div> What?\u2026Going to need some more context to understand this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arch-Magos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509577#post1509577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really beyond me why they did this. Werewolf 5e is already looking like a dumpster fire and I can't wait for the shitshow explosion as mage fans find out about their 5e - Ascension fans are a whole different breed of dedicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026that\u2019s going be a bad time. Going off of the trend, will the Crafts be the main focus as the Traditions and the Technocracy are corrupted from within by Nephandi and consensual reality is removed as a concept?<br /> <br /> So, are these considered successful by Paradox? As a customer, I can\u2019t see these as anything but failures, but I\u2019m not in management or an economics person. Depending on the lesson they learn here, is it possible for them to look towards approving new books for Chronicles, and a better new edition for World?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-25-2023, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T08:51:20-07:00","id":1509589,"title":"","content":"Hey gang, can y'all move the 5th Edition hate to one of the other threads you're already posting to and return this one to the original topic? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T10:22:25-07:00","id":1509596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509589#post1509589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey gang, can y'all move the 5th Edition hate to one of the other threads you're already posting to and return this one to the original topic? Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, this topic has been done to death.<br /> <br /> Let's go back to a question I raised a few pages ago-would we want to see this hypothetical spiritual successor keep to the iconics of vampires, werewolves, wizards, fairies, ghosts, hunters, mummies, and demons? If so, did we want to see them also see the new ones that Chronicles went into, including Frankenstein-style monsters, mythic monsters, and weird psychic/body horror abberations? What would be a take different from the the ones that have been done twice that you think would be interesting?*<br /> <br /> If not, how would you change the line up of concepts? Lean into larger archetypalism (Instead of vampires, mummies, and [reinterpretting them] Frankenstein monsters, a book of the dead living among the living, and a book of shapeshifters, damners, etc.?), or perhaps try and start building from modern horror icons and working backwards (instead of trying to figure out Slashers, Slenderman, and the Backrooms into older paradigms, start from the modern horror landscape and work backwards to make the older iconic monsters make sense in those)? Some other option all together?<br /> <br /> *And I do mean a different take for vampires, werewolves, wizards, ghosts, fairies, hunters, mummies and demons only, I don't want this devolving into a Promethean transhumanism or Beast smacktalking mosh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T10:47:40-07:00","id":1509597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509596#post1509596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be a take different from the the ones that have been done twice that you think would be interesting?*</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always wondered about versions of Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage that were taken in the direction of Changeling or Demon in the extent to which they're quite radically different takes on the same basic concept.<br /> <br /> To give an example, I've wondered about a version of vampire closer to the basic form of Kindred of the East, in that you're not turned into a vampire by another vampire, its something closer to a revenant of folklore.<br /> <br /> Similiarly, I'm curious to see what a Werewolf game that ditched the shamanism would look like?<br /> <br /> Hell, a take on Mage that did something different to iterating on the mechanics of <i>Ars Magica</i> might be interesting (Not saying I dislike free-form magic, just, Awakening feels like the mechanics probably preceded the setting.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T11:00:49-07:00","id":1509600,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting to hit modern stuff instead of the older landscape. It would be pretty helpful to make it different from wod/cofd as well.<br /> <br /> Though the main question for that is what would it look like? <br /> <br /> Admittedly I've rarely touched the modern horror landscape with exceptions (Magnus Archives, Analog horror, SCP) so I don't really know what the modern horror landscape looks like completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T11:29:28-07:00","id":1509603,"title":"","content":"It's somewhat of a question of how much fantasy aspects you want to leave in. If you're sticking with the existence of the supernatural are part of the premise, modern horror doesn't change that much from older horror. Things get updated for the times of course, but there isn't some radically different take on supernatural creatures to deal with.<br /> <br /> If you go more &quot;weird&quot; horror with a lot of &quot;could be supernatural, could be mundane without any known explanation,&quot; stuff, you're in a different territory. Though it's a hard territory to build a larger setting around. It works fine in a &quot;hunter&quot; sort of set up where you're humans (maybe enhanced a bit) deal with all this weirdness, but you lose the &quot;play as the monster&quot; side of things if you don't define what the monsters are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T12:28:57-07:00","id":1509611,"title":"","content":"I'd like to keep Frankenstein's monsters/golems...but I think there might be a neat way we could mix that with the ghost/ dead among the living. I guess I would have the golems explore what it means to live, maybe asking themselves if they are even living in the first place, and I'd have ghosts explore what it means to die...but the concepts are not unrelated. Actually, I guess I would break it down into New Life (Promethean), a Fragment of a Life as it's own entity(Fetch), a Warped and Twisted Life(Remade), and the fading remains of a Life(Ghost). Might be a bit much for one gameline now that I type this down, but I think the themes are connectable....If they end up being their own game lines, I'd like Fetches or something like them to be playable. I don't know, I think it would be fun for a gameline of things that think they are human until they realize that they are only pieces of one.<br /> <br /> I'd probably remove demons as its own line. I'd rather wrap their archetype into fairies, or mythical monsters. Honestly, I'd also involve Mage with Hunter, as people who embrace the supernatural, and people who reject it. Both are humans who regularly interact with the supernatural, and it makes some sense to me that they would be related.<br /> <br /> Mythic monsters in my mind should be where most of the modern horror comes in. Base a lot of it on ancient myths, modern urban legends, and some of the weirder bits of semi-modern psychology in one big mess. For example I really like the idea that Beasts are embodiments of Id, whereas Heroes are embodiments of Super Ego, (and neither make a functional mind alone). I think a further exploration of themes like that would be cool.<br /> <br /> I'd like mummies or an equivalent to continue that non-linear time-jumping thing that specifically isn't in their control. That's a really cool way to explore immortality for a tabletop game. I don't know, I think there is a lot of potential there.<br /> <br /> Going to be honest, no idea of what to do with vampire or werewolf.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T12:34:50-07:00","id":1509615,"title":"","content":"Honestly the thing I'd do is start with anything other than the WoD big three. I like vampires, shifters, and mages, but l think starting with something else could help establish a new identity. Combining it with a move away from gothic horror and gothic punk might help as well.<br /> <br /> I think I'd start with Experiments (I.e.Deviant), Cultists, and other options that lend a strong Conspiracy Horror vibe. Probably including a line which is basically 'hunter under a different name&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T12:39:50-07:00","id":1509617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509615#post1509615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly the thing I'd do is start with anything other than the WoD big three. I like vampires, shifters, and mages, but l think starting with something else could help establish a new identity. Combining it with a move away from gothic horror and gothic punk might help as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, this. This is important. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T12:47:38-07:00","id":1509621,"title":"","content":"Personal opinion, I feel gameline saturation. I would prefer consolidating gamelines (my candidates for deletion would be Beast and Geist, but keeping the underworld lore).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T13:09:57-07:00","id":1509625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509621#post1509621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personal opinion, I feel gameline saturation. I would prefer consolidating gamelines (my candidates for deletion would be Beast and Geist, but keeping the underworld lore).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Deletion isn't the thing for debate, because the hypothetical is OPP doing it's own urban horror game. It's not &quot;How to redo Chronicles or WOrld&quot;, it's &quot;What's something new that would be cool.&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: Or, to put it this way, this conversation is not predicated on picking and choosing things to delete-it's the entire Chronicles of Darkness being dropped, deleted if you will, and hammering out something new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-25-2023, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T13:55:36-07:00","id":1509628,"title":"","content":"For whatever new idea that's coming out I do feel like hunter or at the very least the idea of hunter is going to stick around whatever new urban horror idea of onyxpath ever plans on doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T09:18:39-07:00","id":1510093,"title":"","content":"I'd back a KS for a new urban horror/fantasy line by OPP, as long as it wasn't limited to playing as mortals. Scion exists, yes, but I'm not really a fan of the way that universe is set up.<br /> <br /> That said, I plan to keep playing CofD for a long time - some of the STV content for it is just as good as official published material, and that sort of thing isn't blocked by Paradox (yet).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T06:53:40-07:00","id":1510197,"title":"","content":"There's also They Came From Beyond The Grave, though that has the twin issues that the protagonists are humans and not monsters, and that the whole tone of the thing is affectionate mockery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T07:28:38-07:00","id":1510199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1509615#post1509615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly the thing I'd do is start with anything other than the WoD big three. I like vampires, shifters, and mages, but l think starting with something else could help establish a new identity. Combining it with a move away from gothic horror and gothic punk might help as well.<br /> <br /> I think I'd start with Experiments (I.e.Deviant), Cultists, and other options that lend a strong Conspiracy Horror vibe. Probably including a line which is basically 'hunter under a different name&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd be more inclined to do something that resembles Contagion Chronicles as the baseline: that is, a setting where various different kinds of monsters coexist by default, rather than each type being treated as if it exists in near-complete isolation from the others. Perhaps do it in a manner vaguely similar to an urban fantasy version of Exalted Essence, followed up by a series of \u201cfatsplats\u201d for each of the kinds of supernatural protagonists that the core book makes available; and from there, start introducing other \u201cfatsplats\u201d that <i>aren't </i>covered in the core book. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T19:02:39-07:00","id":1510451,"title":"","content":"Well, since the Monday Meeting brought up the topic, let's talk about how horrifying a hypothetical urban horror game by OPP should be.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned in the comment section, while I think World and Chronicles set a pretty comfortable bar for horror that is good for exploring humanity, if I had to suggest a direction for deviation from those two, I'd rather see the setting get darker, deeper, and scarier as opposed to kicking for the surface.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-01-2023, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T19:07:26-07:00","id":1510452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1510451#post1510451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, since the Monday Meeting brought up the topic, let's talk about how horrifying a hypothetical urban horror game by OPP should be.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned in the comment, while I think World and Chronicles set a pretty comfortable bar for horror that is good for exploring humanity, if I had to suggest a direction for deviation from those two, I'd rather see the setting get darker, deeper, and scarier as opposed to kicking for the surface.</div> </div> </div> </div>i worry a little that might diminish the character's power level. because it's hard to make things scary if you're not powerless. can a game still be scary if my player character is a sexy vampire,or a badass werewollf or mind breaking wizard?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T19:27:40-07:00","id":1510454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506777-if-opp-couldn-t-make-new-cofd-content-should-they-make-a-new-urban-fantasy-line?p=1510452#post1510452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i worry a little that might diminish the character's power level. because it's hard to make things scary if you're not powerless. can a game still be scary if my player character is a sexy vampire,or a badass werewollf or mind breaking wizard?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scary is a matter of perspective, and this sort of take both ignores personal horror, pyschological horror, and fatalistic horror. THere's a lot of ways a story can be scary.<br /> <br /> I mean, on the subject of fatalistic horror, Alan Wake proved how effective it can be to let you know that the spoops were coming way in advance over a decade ago, with a significant portion of that horror being that you could try all you want, you were still always going to run into it. Control, as a comparable contrast for horror against powerful protagonists, was a game that had Jesse Faden becoming an absolute wrecking ball of psychic energy and eldritch gunplay, but constantly keeps you off guard as her by making it clear just how much of her power was luckily* set against the Hiss, making it clear just how thin her defense was against the exceptional, and still finding new ways to mechanically overwhelm the player as it escalated (and often just by virtue of the narrative tensions!).<br /> <br /> Again, just a lot of ways to go about it.<br /> <br /> *Like Alan hasn't been re-engineering reality for the past decade or so, but whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T20:59:09-07:00","id":1510554,"title":"","content":"understood,thanks Kells","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}